{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And her two sons, of whom the name of the one was Gershom</b> — Even though this is not the place of their birth, it explains the names of the sons, for there was no occasion to mention the name Eliezer at his birth, as I explained in the portion of <i>Ve'eleh Shemot</i> (Exodus 4:20). And here it wanted to mention the kindness that the Holy One, blessed be He, did for Moses — that he was a stranger in a foreign land — and to give a name of thanksgiving to HaShem who delivered him from the sword of Pharaoh when he fled, and now he is king over Israel and drowned Pharaoh and his people in the sea. And the sense of <b>“For he said”</b> is connected back to Moses mentioned in the first verse, and likewise <b>“the name of the one was Eliezer, for the Elohim of my father was my help”</b> is connected to “for he said,” and there are many such cases."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:09:58.108060709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}